[{:db/id 17592186152382 :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\overset{A-5I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A-5I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A-5I\\,}{\\to }0 \\\\ x\\overset{\\,\\,\\,A\\,\\,\\,\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{\\,\\,\\,A\\,\\,\\,\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the action of the matrices $A-5I$ and $A$ on the nonzero vectors $u,v,w,x$ and $y$ as depicted above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $v$ is a generalized  eigenvector of rank $2$  corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =5$ of $A$\n\nII. $y$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =0$ of $A$\n\nIII. $u$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $4$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =5$ of $A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186412998 :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }v\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }w\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }0 \\\\ x\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }y\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the action of the matrices $A+3I$ and $A-3I$ on the nonzero vectors $u,v,w,x$ and $y$ as depicted above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A$\n\nII. $u$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ of $A$\n\nIII. $y$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247002 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$\n\nII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$\n\nIII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247013 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2$ of $A$\n\nII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2$ of $A$\n\nIII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-2$ of $A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247016 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A$\n\nII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A$\n\nIII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a709859d-ebd8-5943-9d11-a9e7d7df3f7b" :activity/id #uuid "a709859d-ebd8-5943-9d11-a9e7d7df3f7b" :activity/title "Generalized Eigenvectors" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049408 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-f6d6dca3-2180-5d58-90e6-5c5ae7a5a3ef" "step-af00e671-378f-5ae3-95bf-22f18e729b56" "step-5fcf7480-bb6d-551f-bed4-edf70898be3d" "step-33739050-145e-5afa-87ac-beb7499e226a" "step-4ffd44fb-40d1-534f-9793-15a7bf6ec9e8"] :activity/first-step "step-f6d6dca3-2180-5d58-90e6-5c5ae7a5a3ef" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-f6d6dca3-2180-5d58-90e6-5c5ae7a5a3ef" :step/id #uuid "f6d6dca3-2180-5d58-90e6-5c5ae7a5a3ef" :step/content 17592186152